%C - grab frames from a USB (UVC) camera and show them on HDMI

Syntax:
%C [options]

Options:
   -d index    Camera index (default 0)
   -w width    Frame width to ask the camera for   } default: whatever the
   -h height   Frame height to ask the camera for  } camera driver selects
   -f format   Pixel format to ask for and to assume when displaying:
               yuy2, uyvy, y8, y16 (default: driver's choice, layout guessed)
   -n count    Stop after this many frames (default: run until killed)
   -o file     Save the first frame, raw as received, to this file
   -x          Do not open the framebuffer (probe / save only)
   -v          Driver verbosity; repeat for descriptor dumps (see slog2info)

Uses the SDP's libcapture-usb-uvc.so on top of io-usb-otg, and the firmware
framebuffer for display. The picture is shown 1:1 in greyscale (luma only),
cropped to the screen. Start with:  %C -v -n 5
